This is an UNRELEASED source-package pilot, not an archive submission.
The source is built with distro setuptools through pybuild, without pip,
GitHub binaries, network resolution or feature removal.

/usr/bin/shuttle and /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/shuttle belong to dpkg.
The package installs no service, timer, cron job, /etc conffile, signing key,
credential, user or system state directory. It never calls a live Quipu service
at install, upgrade, remove or purge. Explicit CLI use may create user state at
~/.local/state/shuttle (SHUTTLE_STATE_DIR) and keys at ~/.config/shuttle/keys
(SHUTTLE_KEY_DIR). Both remove and purge leave these user-owned files alone.
Back up and delete them explicitly only when their owner intends to do so.
An upgrade preserves them and runs no migration. Rollback must retain compatible
state; backward compatibility is not implied by a successful dpkg downgrade.

No self-updater is supplied by shuttle. Use APT for files owned by this package.
Quipu and external tracker adapters are separately configured integrations,
not implicitly downloaded packages or package-maintainer-script actions.

The Debian package CI builds from source in an unshare trixie amd64 chroot,
runs lintian and installed-cli autopkgtest, and checks install/reinstall/remove/
purge in fresh containers. A second build compares binary package bytes. Build
logs, packages, lintian findings and comparison hashes are retained as CI artifacts.
This checks the supplied source and distro inputs; it is not archive admission,
a cross-version upgrade test or independent arm64 execution qualification.
An additional container-only lifecycle control upgrades to a synthetic newer
Debian revision of the same application bytes, removes, reinstalls and purges
it. It checks dpkg ownership, retained synthetic user state/signing-key hashes,
and IP network syscalls during package operations and offline CLI controls.
The synthetic revision is never published. This does not test migration between
different application versions or state formats.
The installed manual page is available as shuttle(1). The appointed packaging
maintainer is Intigraph Packaging <packaging@intigraph.ai>; the copyright holder
is Steve Brown. No external submission is authorized here.
